      "writtenOn": "2026-02-12T04:19:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "All the formatters, as far as I investigated, are called in [a for loop with the same arguments](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/tools/depot_tools/+/main:git_cl.py;l\u003d7461-7466;drc\u003d6332e0fb2f483c823d87925061624b2f331f91b2), so they should have the same type, and their argument types can be inferred from what are passed.\n\nSince the first argument is the result of `optparse.OptionParser`, its type is [`optparse.Values`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/optparse.html#optparse.Values). \n\nThe fourth argument is `diffs`, coming from the second return value of [`_FindFilesToFormat`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/tools/depot_tools/+/main:git_cl.py;l\u003d7284-7304;drc\u003d6332e0fb2f483c823d87925061624b2f331f91b2). This value in turn is either the return value of `_SplitDiffsByFile` (`Dict[str, str]`) or `None`.",
      "parentUuid": "83caa829_d7d184bb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7300,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 7300,
        "endChar": 65
